L.5  THE PROTOCOL CAN FAIL

    PASS  the methods are implemented independently of the RL modules   [methods.py imports neither resolution.py nor production.py, so a classical method cannot be the RL mechanism under another name]
    PASS  the methods disagree with one another on their own counters   [identical counters across methods would mean one procedure had been written several times: decisions [0, 22, 11, 22]]
    PASS  the model-set comparison is not an identity on its own argument   [the committed set is the reference, and it is non-empty]
    PASS  a method returning the wrong model set would be reported   [the comparison in L.1 is against the committed set]

